{"id":229900155707282,"type":"album","name":"Perfect From Now On","artist":"Built To Spill","year":1997,"weight":57,"info":{"cover":"https://dn711000.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-a253ff2f-c934-4801-822a-5b476268ba36/mbid-a253ff2f-c934-4801-822a-5b476268ba36-22152232964.jpg","kind":"Album","tracks":6,"country":"US","scaruffi":8.5,"yt":"FsTl-lZo_50","links":{"spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/album/6DlZzUnITGI5cWGTjIWSBm","youtube":"https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=OLAK5uy_m0oJBryfJZJtV5z5B0Q0vzq0VvR026eb0"},"desc":"Perfect from Now On is the third full-length album released by Built to Spill, and the band's first major label (Warner Bros.) release. The line-up for the album was singer/guitarist Doug Martsch, bassist Brett Nelson, and drummer Scott Plouf. It was recorded at the Avast! Recording Company in Seattle, Washington by Phil Ek. Stylistically, the album was marked by its experimentation with longer song structures, philosophical lyrics, and the incorporation of cello. The album was essentially recorded three times. The first time, Martsch attempted to play all the instruments except drums. He and Phil Ek were dissatisfied with the results, ."},"artist_ref":{"id":237764272115141,"name":"Built To Spill","info":{"img":"https://cdn-images.dzcdn.net/images/artist/28f673c966851c245f7463e2630aee89/1000x1000-000000-80-0-0.jpg"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":185670346256268,"type":"genre","name":"rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":3782,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":8412226417108,"type":"genre","name":"Indie Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":1139,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"},{"id":191826593279813,"type":"genre","name":"Art Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":531,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"},{"id":245950225873330,"type":"genre","name":"Post-Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":526,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":237890000566646,"type":"genre","name":"Post-Hardcore","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":341,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},